  "body": "The test `fig8_pocket_outside_starts_each_level_at_the_stock_edge` took 961 s in a debug quick-gate run. It tripped the gate's 15-minute stall watchdog. The step `app suites: pocket_pass_start` then reads as a stall. Every gate that reaches this test stops there.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- PR #3577, quick gate `gate-logs/quick-20261122-233747`, step `app suites: pocket_pass_start`: killed at 961 s by the stall watchdog (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_STALL_MIN`, 15 min).\n- A test that takes more than about 60 s in debug belongs in a heavy lane (its ignore reason names the lane) or on a smaller fixture.\n\n## What to do\n\n- Move the test to a heavy lane, or reduce its fixture, and keep its asserts.\n- Record the debug and release run times.\n- Check the other app suites for the same latency class.\n\nThe 60-minute stall cap is not the fix. The cap only diagnoses.\n\n## Related\n\n- #3577: the change that reaches this test.\n- #3581: the test-tool follow-up.\n",
